.TH "ROARK\-SIMULATION\-GROUP\-RUN" "1" "" "roark-simulation-group-run" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-simulation\-group\-run \- Run a simulation group
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark simulation group run
\fIgroup\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Starts one run of every plan in the group, exactly as POST /v1/simulation/plan/{planId}/job would for each, and groups the runs into a run group whose combined report is announced through the group's notification settings once it is ready. This places real calls. Config\-managed groups can be run here too. Returns the run group. Poll GET /v1/simulation/run\-group/{groupId} until `latestReport.status` is READY. If a plan cannot start after others did, the runs that started are still grouped and the 400 names the run group id.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/simulation/group/{groupId}/run
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIgroup\-id\fR
The simulation group ID
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
